{"slug":"14-0-ratios-rates-proportional-relationships-and-units","title":"14.0 Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","subject":"MATH","total":57,"questions":[{"id":17611,"html":"<p>For a person <i>m</i> miles from a flash of lightning, the length of the time interval from the moment the person sees the lightning to the moment the person hears the thunder is k seconds. The ratio of m to k can be estimated to be 1 to 5. According to this estimate, the person is how many miles from a flash of lightning if the time interval is 25 seconds?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66488,"html":"<p>10</p>","correct":false},{"id":66489,"html":"<p>9</p>","correct":false},{"id":66490,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":false},{"id":66491,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17612,"html":"<p>A group of monarch butterflies migrated from Chicago, Illinois, to Michoacán, Mexico, flying a total of 2,100 miles. It took a single butterfly in the group 120 days to travel this route one way. On average, how many miles did the butterfly travel per day?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66492,"html":"<p>0.057</p>","correct":false},{"id":66493,"html":"<p>0.729</p>","correct":false},{"id":66494,"html":"<p>17.5</p>","correct":true},{"id":66495,"html":"<p>24</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17613,"html":"<p>In a box of pens, the ratio of black pens to red pens is 8 to 1. There are 40 black pens in the box. How many red pens are in the box?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66496,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":true},{"id":66497,"html":"<p>8</p>","correct":false},{"id":66498,"html":"<p>40</p>","correct":false},{"id":66499,"html":"<p>120</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17614,"html":"<p>The population density of Worthington is 290 people per square mile. Worthington has a population of 92,800 people. What is the area, in square miles, of Worthington?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66500,"html":"<p>102,400</p>","correct":false},{"id":66501,"html":"<p>93,090</p>","correct":false},{"id":66502,"html":"<p>320</p>","correct":true},{"id":66503,"html":"<p>32</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17615,"html":"<p>A wind turbine completes 900 revolutions in 50 minutes. At this rate, how many revolutions per minute does this turbine complete?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66504,"html":"<p>18</p>","correct":true},{"id":66505,"html":"<p>850</p>","correct":false},{"id":66506,"html":"<p>950</p>","correct":false},{"id":66507,"html":"<p>1,400</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17616,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/WZhCCyYqoOMnYGUoEkGP3J1aPItXS1l35eyVUqoL.png\" style=\"width: 263px;\"><br><br>In the table above, the ratio of y to x for each ordered pair is constant. What is the value of k?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66508,"html":"<p>28</p>","correct":false},{"id":66509,"html":"<p>36</p>","correct":false},{"id":66510,"html":"<p>80</p>","correct":false},{"id":66511,"html":"<p>160</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17617,"html":"<p>The ratio of t to u is 1 to 2, and t = 10. What is the value of u?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66512,"html":"<p>2</p>","correct":false},{"id":66513,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":false},{"id":66514,"html":"<p>10</p>","correct":false},{"id":66515,"html":"<p>20</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17618,"html":"<p>How many <u>yards</u> are equivalent to 612 inches? (1 yard = 36 inches)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66516,"html":"<p>0.059</p>","correct":false},{"id":66517,"html":"<p>17</p>","correct":true},{"id":66518,"html":"<p>576</p>","correct":false},{"id":66519,"html":"<p>22,032</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17619,"html":"<p>Shaquan has 7 red cards and 28 blue cards. What is the ratio of red cards to blue cards that Shaquan has?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66520,"html":"<p>1 to 4</p>","correct":true},{"id":66521,"html":"<p>4 to 1</p>","correct":false},{"id":66522,"html":"<p>1 to 7</p>","correct":false},{"id":66523,"html":"<p>7 to 1</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17620,"html":"<p>A cherry pitting machine pits 12 pounds of cherries in 3 minutes. At this rate, how many minutes does it take the machine to pit 96 pounds of cherries?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66524,"html":"<p>8</p>","correct":false},{"id":66525,"html":"<p>15</p>","correct":false},{"id":66526,"html":"<p>24</p>","correct":true},{"id":66527,"html":"<p>36</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17621,"html":"<p>A kangaroo has a mass of 28 kilograms. What is the kangaroo's mass, in grams? (1 kilogram = 1,000 grams)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66528,"html":"<p>28,000</p>","correct":true},{"id":66529,"html":"<p>1,028</p>","correct":false},{"id":66530,"html":"<p>972</p>","correct":false},{"id":66531,"html":"<p>784</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17622,"html":"<p>An object travels at a constant speed of 12 centimeters per second. At this speed, what is the time, in seconds, that it would take for the object to travel 108 centimeters?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":fal