correct":false},{"id":66582,"html":"<p>125,312</p>","correct":false},{"id":66583,"html":"<p>80,200</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17635,"html":"<p>Rectangle A has length 15 and width w. Rectangle B has length 20 and the same length-to-width ratio as rectangle A. What is the width of rectangle B in terms of w?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66584,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{4}{3}w</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02691em;\">w</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":true},{"id":66585,"html":"<p>w + 5</p>","correct":false},{"id":66586,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{3}{4}w</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02691em;\">w</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":66587,"html":"<p>w - 5</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17636,"html":"<p>Tanya earns $13.50 per hour at her part-time job. When she works z hours, she earns 13.50z dollars. Which of the following expressions gives the amount, in dollars, Tanya will earn if she works 3z hours?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66588,"html":"<p>3(13.50z)</p>","correct":true},{"id":66589,"html":"<p>3 + 13.50z&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66590,"html":"<p>3z + 13.50 z&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66591,"html":"<p>13.50(z + 3)</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17637,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/xluwfRagSqAlkzmWZcJENOviraqP2pTrATawUsdC.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: auto;\"><br><br>The glass pictured above can hold a maximum volume of 473 cubic centimeters, which is approximately 16 fluid ounces. Jenny has a pitcher that contains 1 gallon of water. How many times could Jenny completely fill the glass with 1 gallon of water? (1 gallon = 128 fluid ounces)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66592,"html":"<p>16</p>","correct":false},{"id":66593,"html":"<p>8</p>","correct":true},{"id":66594,"html":"<p>4</p>","correct":false},{"id":66595,"html":"<p>3</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17638,"html":"<p>Which of the following speeds is equivalent to 90 kilometers per hour? (1 kilometer = 1,000 meters)&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66596,"html":"<p>25 meters per second&nbsp;</p>","correct":true},{"id":66597,"html":"<p>32 meters per second</p>","correct":false},{"id":66598,"html":"<p>250 meters per second</p>","correct":false},{"id":66599,"html":"<p>324 meters per second</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17639,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/naF0IVIEcYrUVouvH8UWd6VAxSSaun6AVmRyosSV.png\" style=\"width: 373px;\"><br><br>The table above shows the amount of protein in two foods and the cost of each food. Based on the table, what is the ratio of the cost per gram of protein in a large egg to the cost per gram of protein in a cup of milk?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66600,"html":"<p>1 : 2</p>","correct":false},{"id":66601,"html":"<p>2 : 3</p>","correct":false},{"id":66602,"html":"<p>3 : 4</p>","correct":false},{"id":66603,"html":"<p>2 : 1</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17640,"html":"<p>The total area of a coastal city is 92.1 square miles, of which 11.3 square miles is water. If the city had a population of 621,000 people in the year 2010, which of the following is closest to the population density, in people per square mile of land area, of the city at that time?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66604,"html":"<p>6,740</p>","correct":false},{"id":66605,"html":"<p>7,690</p>","correct":true},{"id":66606,"html":"<p>55,000</p>","correct":false},{"id":66607,"html":"<p>76,000</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17641,"html":"<p>d = 55t <br><br>The equation above can be used to calculate the distance d, in miles, traveled by a car moving at a speed of 55 miles per hour over a period of t hours. For any positive constant k, the distance the car would have traveled after 9k hours is how many times the distance the car would have traveled after 3k hours?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66608,"html":"<p>3</p>","correct":true},{"id":66609,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":false},{"id":66610,"html":"<p>3k</p>","correct":false},{"id":66611,"html":"<p>6k</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17642,"html":"<p>For a certain rectangular region, the ratio of its length to its width is 35 to 10. If the width of the rectangular region increases by 7 units, how must the length change to maintain this ratio?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66612,"html":"<p>It must decrease by 24.5 units.&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66613,"html":"<p>It must increase by 24.5 units.&nbsp;</p>","correct":true},{"id":66614,"html":"<p>It must decrease by 7 units.&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66615,"html":"<p>It must increase by 7 units.</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17643,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/rt5GztpxDxczCELHjxwK77b1jUZzQopEi08vVH0N.png\" style=\"width: 302px;\"><br><br>One method of calculating the approximate age, in years, of a tree of a particular species is to multiply the diameter of the tree, in inches, by a constant called the growth factor for that species. The table above gives the growth factors for eight species of trees. If a white birch tree and a pin oak tree each now have a diameter of 1 foot, which of the following will be closest to the difference, in inches, of their diameters 10 years from now? (1 foot = 12 inches)&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66616,"html":"<p>1.0</p>","correct":false},{"id":66617,"html":"<p>1.2</p>","correct":false},{"id":66618,"html":"<p>1.3</p>","correct":true},{"id":66619,"html":"<p>1.4</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17644,"html":"<p>A sample of oak has a density of 807 kilograms per cubic meter. The sample is in the shape of a cube, where each edge has a length of 0.90 meters. To the nearest whole number, what is the mass, in kilograms, of this sample?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66620,"html":"<p>588</p>","correct":true},{"id":66621,"html":"<p>726</p>","correct":false},{"id":66622,"html":"<p>897</p>","correct":false},{"id":66623,"html":"<p>1,107</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17645,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/rghPngg2ZetQOg1wuf8pw4hCnHMp32mOfQyxJXF8.png\" style=\"width: 573px;\"><br><br>The table shows the distribution, by location and power capacity (maximum rate of power generation) of the twenty largest wind projects in the United States in 2013. The total power capacity of the nine wind projects located in Texas was 4,952 megawatts (MW), and the total power capacity of the twenty wind projects was 11,037 MW in 2013. The amount of energy produced in one hour at a rate of one megawatt is one megawatt-hour. If each of the nine Texas wind projects in 2013 had operated continuously for 24 hours at the maximum rate of power generation, approximately how many megawatt-hours of energy would the nine projects have produced?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66624,"html":"<p>200</p>","correct":false},{"id":66625,"html":"<p>5,000</p>","correct":false},{"id":66626,"html":"<p>11,000</p>","correct":false},{"id":66627,"html":"<p>120,000</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17646,"html":"<p>The density of a certain type of wood is 353 kilograms per cubic meter. A sample of this type of wood is in the shape of a cube and has a mass of 345 kilograms. To the nearest hundredth of a meter, what is the length of one edge of this sample?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66628,"html":"<p>0.98</p>","correct":false},{"id":66629,"html":"<p>0.99</p>","correct":true},{"id":66630,"html":"<p>1.01</p>","correct":false},{"id":66631,"html":"<p>1.02</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17647,"html":"<p>A certain town has an area of 4.36 square miles. What is the area, in square yards, of this town? (1 mile = 1,760 yards)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66632,"html":"<p>404</p>","correct":false},{"id":66633,"html":"<p>7,674</p>","correct":false},{"id":66634,"html":"<p>710,459</p>","correct":false},{"id":66635,"html":"<p>13,505,536</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17648,"html":"<p>Anita created a batch of green paint by mixing 2 ounces of blue paint with 3 ounces of yellow paint. She must mix a second batch using the same ratio of blue and yellow paint as the first batch. If she uses 5 ounces of blue paint for the second batch, how much yellow paint should Anita use?&nbsp;</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66636,"html":"<p>Exactly 5 ounces&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66637,"html":"<p>3 ounces more than the amount of yellow paint used in the first batch&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66638,"html":"<p>1.5 times the amount of yellow paint used in the first batch&nbsp;</p>","correct":false},{"id":66639,"html":"<p>1.5 times the amount of blue paint used in the second batch</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17649,"html":"<p>A certain park has an area of 11,863,808 square yards. What is the area, in square miles, of this park? (1 mile = 1,760 yards)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":66640,"html":"<p>1.96</p>","correct":false},{"id":66641,"html":"<p>3.83</p>","correct":true},{"id":66642,"html":"<p>3,444.39</p>","correct":false},{"id":66643,"html":"<p>6,740.8</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17650,"html":"<p>A printer produces posters at a constant rate of 42 posters per minute. At what rate, in posters per <u>hour</u>, does the printer produce the posters?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"2,520","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17651,"html":"<p>A customer spent $27 to purchase oranges at $3 per pound. How many pounds of oranges did the customer purchase?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"9","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17652,"html":"<p>A special camera is used for underwater ocean research. When the camera is at a depth of 58 fathoms, what is the camera's depth in feet? (1 fathom = 6 feet)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"348","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17653,"html":"<p>How many feet are equivalent to 34 yards? (1 yard = 3 feet)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"102","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17654,"html":"<p>If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{x}{y}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1765em;vertical-align:-0.4811em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6954em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4811em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;= 4 and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{24x}{ny}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3262em;vertical-align:-0.4811em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">24</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4811em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;= 4, what is the value of n?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"24","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17655,"html":"<p>Pure beeswax has a density of 0.555 ounce per cubic inch. An online company sells pure beeswax at a price of $8.00 per ounce. What is the selling price, in dollars per cubic inch, for pure beeswax purchased from this company?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"4.44","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17656,"html":"<p>On April 18, 1775, Paul Revere set off on his midnight ride from Charlestown to Lexington. If he had ridden straight to Lexington without stopping, he would have traveled 11 miles in 26 minutes. In such a ride, what would the average speed of his horse have been, to the nearest tenth of a mile per <u>hour</u>?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"25.4","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17657,"html":"<p>One of a planet's moons orbits the planet every 252 days. A second moon orbits the planet every 287 days. How many more days does it take the second moon to orbit the planet 29 times than it takes the first moon to orbit the planet 29 times?</p>","description":"<p><br></p>","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"1,015","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17658,"html":"<p>A distance of 61 furlongs is equivalent to how many feet? (1 furlong = 220 yards and 1 yard = 3 feet)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"40,260","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17659,"html":"<p>The population density of Cedar County is 230 people per square mile. The county has a population of 85,100 people. What is the area, in square miles, of Cedar County?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"370","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17660,"html":"<p>A distance of 112 furlongs is equivalent to how many feet? (1 furlong = 220 yards and 1 yard = 3 feet)</p>","description":"<p><br></p>","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"73,920","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17661,"html":"<p>For the values j and k, the ratio of j to k is 11 to 12. If j is multiplied by 17, what is k multiplied by in order to maintain the same ratio?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"17","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17662,"html":"<p>How many <u>tablespoons</u> are equivalent to 14 teaspoons? (3 teaspoons = 1 tablespoon)</p>","description":"<p><br></p>","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"14/3","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17663,"html":"<p>A triathlon is a multisport race consisting of three different legs. A triathlon participant completed the cycling leg with an average speed of 19.700 miles per hour. What was the average speed, in <u>yards</u> per hour, of the participant during the cycling leg? (1 mile = 1,760 yards)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"34,672","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17664,"html":"<p>One side of a flat board has an area of 874 square inches. If a pressure of 19 pounds per square inch of area is exerted on this side of the board, what is the total force, in pounds, exerted on this side of the board?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"16,606","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17665,"html":"<p>A competition consisted of four different events. One participant completed the first event with an average speed of 20.300 miles per hour. What was this average speed, in yards per hour? (1 mile = 1,760 yards)</p>","description":"<p><br></p>","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"35,728","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17666,"html":"<p>Jeremy deposited x dollars in his investment account on January 1, 2001. The amount of money in the account doubled each year until Jeremy had 480 dollars in his investment account on January 1, 2005. What is the value of x?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":"30","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":17667,"html":"<p>If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{4a}{b}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;= 6.7 and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>26.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{a}{bn}=26.8</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0404em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6954em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">bn</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">26.8</span></span></span></span>, what is the value of n?</p>","description":"<p><br></p>","explanation":"","type":"saq","answer":".0625","options":[],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false}]}